@mobile_link
Duskwright is desktop Chrome only. Learn more

@store_listing
Duskwright creates dark themes for websites on the fly — without ever writing to the page. Unlike typical dark-mode extensions, it cannot leave stray styling inside your documents, so a spreadsheet or doc you view stays exactly as you left it.

You can adjust the brightness, contrast, sepia filter, dark mode, font settings, and the ignore list.

When a site can't be themed automatically, Duskwright tells you instead of failing silently, and an element picker lets you darken any region by hand. There are Developer Tools for experienced users.

Duskwright shows no ads, has no telemetry, and sends your data nowhere. It's fully open source: https://github.com/blamechris/duskwright  It is a fork of Dark Reader, used under the MIT License, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Dark Reader Ltd.

Before you install it, disable similar extensions. Enjoy watching!
